WEBVTT

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.454
The other key challenge of virtual teams
is shared understanding,

00:11:02.478 --> 00:11:04.476
being able to get on the same page,

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.072
not just about what you're doing,

00:11:06.096 --> 00:11:08.865
but also about who you are
and what you value.

00:11:08.889 --> 00:11:12.560
MH: It's basically the problem that you
kind of have incomplete information.

00:11:12.584 --> 00:11:17.006
You don't have a good understanding
of each other's contexts, right?

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:20.036
So this is actually why
it's really valuable

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:24.243
to ask members of your remote team,
"What does your workplace look like?

00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:26.030
Who else is there? Do you have a dog?

00:11:26.054 --> 00:11:28.626
Are you watching your kid?
What else is going on?"

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.916
AG: You know you've reached
shared understanding